          "short": "$-6\\frac{3}{7},\\ -\\frac{11}{3},\\ -\\frac{7}{3},\\ \\frac{4}{7},\\ \\frac{5}{7},\\ \\frac{19}{3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\frac{-5}{-7}=\\frac{5}{7}.$$\nExpress the numbers in twenty-firsts and compare their positions on the number line:\n$$-\\frac{135}{21}<-\\frac{77}{21}<-\\frac{49}{21}<\\frac{12}{21}<\\frac{15}{21}<\\frac{133}{21}.$$\nTherefore the increasing order is\n$$-6\\frac{3}{7},\\ -\\frac{11}{3},\\ -\\frac{7}{3},\\ \\frac{4}{7},\\ \\frac{5}{7},\\ \\frac{19}{3}.$$",
